# Git + Firebase is the delivery path

FOAM is reviewed and used on the **live Firebase Hosting site**, not via localhost.

## Required after feature/UI work

1. **Git** — commit relevant changes on the working branch and push to `origin` (`https://github.com/Nokui8i/FOAM`).
2. **Build** — run `npm run build` (static export to `out/`).
3. **Deploy** — `npx firebase deploy --only hosting --project foam-laundry-app`.
4. **Verify** on the live URL: `https://foam-laundry-app.web.app` (and relevant paths like `/`, `/ops`).

## Do not

- Stop at `npm run dev` / localhost as the deliverable for the user.
- Treat localhost screenshots as “done” when the user expects the site online.
- Deploy a separate side host for design-reference repos unless explicitly asked.

## Notes

- Design-only repos (e.g. Lovable / `foam-operations-hub`) are **UI references** to port into this FOAM repo; they are not the production host.
- If the user says not to publish yet, skip deploy — but still prepare Git commits when they ask to save work.
- Prefer the current feature branch for push/deploy unless told to merge to `master`.
